# No rule for /dist/* although webpack.prod.js content-hashes it
# (dist/[name].[contenthash].js). Cloudflare applies _headers to 404
# responses too, and the edge caches them: with an immutable rule here, a
# browser that asks for a bundle in the seconds after a deploy, or for an
# old bundle, keeps that 404 for a year (measured 2026-10-12). The default
# (max-age=0, must-revalidate + ETag) costs only free revalidations.

# Textures, icons and CSS are committed files with stable, unhashed names:
# src/blocks.ts and src/voxelMaterial.ts request them by literal URL, so they
# never go through webpack and never get a hash. A stale one is still wrong,
# so cap the TTL at a day.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/styles/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
